<topic id="theme">
  <title>Theme</title>
  <shortdesc>Combine one of three theme utilities with our theme color classes to set
    color and background-color pairings on any element, just like component variants.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Theme</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Color</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Background</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">

    <section id="overview">
      <title>Overview</title>
      <p>Take any of our theme color classes and add <codeph>theme-contrast</codeph>,
        <codeph>theme-subtle</codeph>, or <codeph>theme-muted</codeph> to set a predefined
        color and background-color pairing. Then optionally add <codeph>theme-border</codeph>
        to set a predefined border color.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="contrast">
      <title>Contrast</title>
      <p>Contrast pairs the bg theme token with the contrast text color for maximum
        readability with <codeph>theme-contrast</codeph>. This is ideal for high-emphasis
        elements with solid backgrounds.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <div outputclass="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <div theme="primary-contrast" padding="2">.theme-primary .theme-contrast</div>
        <div theme="accent-contrast" padding="2">.theme-accent .theme-contrast</div>
        <div theme="success-contrast" padding="2">.theme-success .theme-contrast</div>
        <div theme="danger-contrast" padding="2">.theme-danger .theme-contrast</div>
        <div theme="warning-contrast" padding="2">.theme-warning .theme-contrast</div>
        <div theme="info-contrast" padding="2">.theme-info .theme-contrast</div>
        <div theme="inverse-contrast" padding="2">.theme-inverse .theme-contrast</div>
        <div theme="secondary-contrast" padding="2">.theme-secondary .theme-contrast</div>
      </div>
    </example>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock>&lt;div theme="primary-contrast" padding="2"&gt;.theme-primary .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div theme="accent-contrast" padding="2"&gt;.theme-accent .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div theme="success-contrast" padding="2"&gt;.theme-success .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div theme="danger-contrast" padding="2"&gt;.theme-danger .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div theme="warning-contrast" padding="2"&gt;.theme-warning .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div theme="info-contrast" padding="2"&gt;.theme-info .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div theme="inverse-contrast" padding="2"&gt;.theme-inverse .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div theme="secondary-contrast" padding="2"&gt;.theme-secondary .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;</codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock>&lt;div outputclass="p-2 theme-primary theme-contrast"&gt;.theme-primary .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div outputclass="p-2 theme-accent theme-contrast"&gt;.theme-accent .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div outputclass="p-2 theme-success theme-contrast"&gt;.theme-success .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div outputclass="p-2 theme-danger theme-contrast"&gt;.theme-danger .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div outputclass="p-2 theme-warning theme-contrast"&gt;.theme-warning .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div outputclass="p-2 theme-info theme-contrast"&gt;.theme-info .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div outputclass="p-2 theme-inverse theme-contrast"&gt;.theme-inverse .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div outputclass="p-2 theme-secondary theme-contrast"&gt;.theme-secondary .theme-contrast&lt;/div&gt;</codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

