        <div theme="inverse-subtle" padding="3" rounded="yes" outputclass="flex-fill text-center">Inverse with a
          <xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#">link</xref></div>
        <div theme="inverse-muted" padding="3" rounded="yes" outputclass="flex-fill text-center">Inverse with a
          <xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#">link</xref></div>
      </div>
      <div outputclass="d-flex gap-2 mb-2">
        <div theme="secondary-contrast" padding="3" rounded="yes" outputclass="flex-fill text-center">Secondary with a
          <xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#">link</xref></div>
        <div theme="secondary-subtle" padding="3" rounded="yes" outputclass="flex-fill text-center">Secondary with a
          <xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#">link</xref></div>
        <div theme="secondary-muted" padding="3" rounded="yes" outputclass="flex-fill text-center">Secondary with a
          <xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#">link</xref></div>
      </div>
    </example>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock>&lt;div outputclass="d-flex gap-2" margin="b2"&gt;
  &lt;div theme="primary-contrast" padding="3" rounded="yes" outputclass="flex-fill text-center"&gt;Primary with a
    &lt;xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#"&gt;link&lt;/xref&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div theme="primary-subtle" padding="3" rounded="yes" outputclass="flex-fill text-center"&gt;Primary with a
    &lt;xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#"&gt;link&lt;/xref&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div theme="primary-muted" padding="3" rounded="yes" outputclass="flex-fill text-center"&gt;Primary with a
    &lt;xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#"&gt;link&lt;/xref&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock>&lt;div outputclass="d-flex gap-2 mb-2"&gt;
  &lt;div outputclass="theme-primary theme-contrast p-3 flex-fill text-center rounded"&gt;Primary with a
    &lt;xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#"&gt;link&lt;/xref&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div outputclass="theme-primary theme-subtle p-3 flex-fill text-center rounded"&gt;Primary with a
    &lt;xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#"&gt;link&lt;/xref&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div outputclass="theme-primary theme-muted p-3 flex-fill text-center rounded"&gt;Primary with a
    &lt;xref outputclass="underline-50 hover:underline-100" href="#"&gt;link&lt;/xref&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section id="with-components">
      <title>With components</title>
      <p>Theme utilities work great with components that support theming. Apply the
        theme color to a container and use theme style classes on individual elements.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <div outputclass="theme-primary">
        <div outputclass="d-flex gap-2 mb-3">
          <ph outputclass="badge theme-contrast">Contrast badge</ph>
          <ph outputclass="badge theme-subtle">Subtle badge</ph>
          <ph outputclass="badge theme-muted">Muted badge</ph>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div outputclass="theme-danger">
        <div outputclass="d-flex gap-2 mb-3">
          <ph outputclass="badge theme-contrast">Contrast badge</ph>
          <ph outputclass="badge theme-subtle">Subtle badge</ph>
          <ph outputclass="badge theme-muted">Muted badge</ph>
        </div>
      </div>
    </example>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <p outputclass="text-muted">A bare <codeph>theme-{color}</codeph> container (setting only the CSS
          custom properties for descendants to consume, with no contrast/subtle/muted/border
          suffix of its own) has no <xmlatt>theme</xmlatt> attribute equivalent &#8212; <xmlelement
          >div</xmlelement>'s <xmlatt>theme</xmlatt> enumeration requires a suffix. This case
          still requires <xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt>.</p>
        <codeblock>&lt;div outputclass="theme-primary"&gt;
  &lt;div outputclass="d-flex gap-2 mb-3"&gt;
    &lt;ph outputclass="badge theme-contrast"&gt;Contrast badge&lt;/ph&gt;
    &lt;ph outputclass="badge theme-subtle"&gt;Subtle badge&lt;/ph&gt;
    &lt;ph outputclass="badge theme-muted"&gt;Muted badge&lt;/ph&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock>&lt;div outputclass="theme-primary"&gt;
  &lt;div outputclass="d-flex gap-2 mb-3"&gt;
    &lt;ph outputclass="badge theme-contrast"&gt;Contrast badge&lt;/ph&gt;
    &lt;ph outputclass="badge theme-subtle"&gt;Subtle badge&lt;/ph&gt;
    &lt;ph outputclass="badge theme-muted"&gt;Muted badge&lt;/ph&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <p>You can also mix theme colors within the same container by applying different
      <codeph>theme-{color}</codeph> classes to child elements:</p>
    <example>
      <div outputclass="d-flex gap-2">
        <div theme="success-contrast" padding="3" rounded="yes">Success</div>
        <div theme="warning-contrast" padding="3" rounded="yes">Warning</div>
        <div theme="danger-contrast" padding="3" rounded="yes">Danger</div>
      </div>
    </example>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock>&lt;div outputclass="d-flex gap-2"&gt;
  &lt;div theme="success-contrast" padding="3" rounded="yes"&gt;Success&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div theme="warning-contrast" padding="3" rounded="yes"&gt;Warning&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div theme="danger-contrast" padding="3" rounded="yes"&gt;Danger&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock>&lt;div outputclass="d-flex gap-2"&gt;
  &lt;div outputclass="theme-success theme-contrast p-3 rounded"&gt;Success&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div outputclass="theme-warning theme-contrast p-3 rounded"&gt;Warning&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div outputclass="theme-danger theme-contrast p-3 rounded"&gt;Danger&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section id="how-theme-values-are-built-up">
      <title>How theme values are built up</title>
      <p>Every theme value used throughout this documentation, whether on an individual
        element's <xmlatt>theme</xmlatt> attribute (or the base plugin's <xmlatt
        >outputclass</xmlatt>), or on one of the <parmname>--bootstrap.theme.*</parmname>
        command line parameters below, is a hyphenated compound of one of the 8 Bootstrap
        theme colors:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><codeph>accent</codeph></li>
        <li><codeph>danger</codeph></li>
        <li><codeph>info</codeph></li>
        <li><codeph>inverse</codeph></li>
        <li><codeph>primary</codeph></li>
        <li><codeph>secondary</codeph></li>
        <li><codeph>success</codeph></li>
        <li><codeph>warning</codeph></li>
      </ul>
      <p>With a suffix indicating the theme style</p>
      <ul>
        <li><codeph>-contrast</codeph> pairs the solid background with the contrast text color</li>
        <li><codeph>-subtle</codeph> pairs the low-contrast background with matching text</li>
        <li><codeph>-muted</codeph> pairs the low-contrast background with muted text</li>
        <li><codeph>-border</codeph> sets a predefined border color on its own</li>
        <li><codeph>-subtle-border</codeph> combines <codeph>-subtle</codeph> and <codeph>-border</codeph></li>
      </ul>
      <p>The following command line parameters optionally consume a theme value to style layout regions:</p>
      <parml>
        <plentry>
          <pt><parmname>--bootstrap.theme.header</parmname></pt>
          <pd>Page header theme. Defaults to <option>primary-contrast</option></pd>
        </plentry>
        <plentry>
          <pt><parmname>--bootstrap.theme.footer</parmname></pt>
          <pd>Page footer theme. Defaults to <option>none</option></pd>
        </plentry>
        <plentry>
          <pt><parmname>--bootstrap.theme.sidebar</parmname></pt>
          <pd><xref href="nav.dita#navigation/sidebar"/> theme. Defaults to <option>none</option></pd>
        </plentry>
        <plentry>
          <pt><parmname>--bootstrap.theme.topbar</parmname></pt>
          <pd><xref href="nav.dita#navigation/top-bar"/> theme. Defaults to <option>none</option></pd>
        </plentry>
        <plentry>
          <pt><parmname>--bootstrap.theme.content</parmname></pt>
          <pd>Main content area theme. Defaults to <option>none</option></pd>
        </plentry>
        <plentry>
          <pt><parmname>--bootstrap.theme.scrollspy</parmname></pt>
          <pd><xref href="scrollspy.dita"/> menu theme. Defaults to <option>none</option></pd>
        </plentry>
        <plentry>
          <pt><parmname>--bootstrap.theme.body</parmname></pt>
          <pd>Page <xmlelement>body</xmlelement>. Defaults to
            <option>none</option></pd>
        </plentry>
      </parml>
    </section>

  </body>
</topic>
